litfetch — NOTICE
=================

The package itself is MIT-licensed (see LICENSE).

This file records three separate things, because they carry three different
obligations: ideas taken from other tools, optional third-party code, and the
services the tool talks to.

1. Ideas borrowed (attribution, no code copied)
-----------------------------------------------

No third-party source code is vendored in this repository. The design borrowed
the following ideas, each after a specific failure in the 2026-10 audit:

  * "honest results" — report the route that produced a file and label it
    preprint / accepted manuscript / version of record.
    from: fulltext-article-downloader (computron)
  * fail fast on a challenge or paywall page instead of retrying it.
    from: scihub-cli (Oxidane-bot)
  * resolve a title to a DOI by score and reject a weak match.
    from: DoiHunter (mehmoodulhaq570)
  * skip what is already present, and report "already there" separately from
    "downloaded".  from: DoiHunter, scihub-cli
  * Retry-After and per-host pacing.
    from: scihub-cli; Unpaywall/Crossref terms of use
  * provenance in the item rather than an external database (reading status).
    from: Zotero "reading-list" / "Reading Flow" plugins
  * an optional TLS-fingerprint retry, clearly labelled as a retry rather than a
    solution.  from: fulltext-article-downloader's [tls] extra

2. Optional third-party code (installed by the user, never bundled)
-------------------------------------------------------------------

The wheel contains no third-party code. These are extras:

  extra      package            licence        note
  ---------  -----------------  -------------  --------------------------------
  pdf        PyMuPDF            AGPL-3.0       see the warning below
  browser    websocket-client   Apache-2.0     Chrome DevTools Protocol client
  tls        curl_cffi          MIT            Chrome TLS fingerprint replay
  dev        pytest             MIT            test runner only

  **PyMuPDF is AGPL-3.0, not MIT.** It is an optional extra and is never
  vendored or redistributed here, so this repository stays MIT. But a *combined
  distribution* that bundles PyMuPDF (a frozen app, a container image, an
  all-in-one installer) inherits AGPL-3.0 obligations for that combination. If
  you need to ship such a bundle under a non-AGPL licence, either obtain a
  commercial PyMuPDF licence from Artifex or replace the `pdf` backend.
  The core package runs without it: identity checks then degrade to
  magic-byte and size checks, and `litfetch doctor` says so.

3. Services contacted (their terms, not ours)
---------------------------------------------

  * arXiv API — 3 s between requests, as their terms ask.
  * Crossref, OpenAlex, Unpaywall — metadata APIs; Unpaywall requires a contact
    address (`LITFETCH_MAILTO`). Bulk metadata is not redistributed by this tool.
  * Semantic Scholar, Europe PMC / PMC Open Access — their own terms.
  * Publisher sites — fetched only where the network is already entitled to the
    content. This tool contains no paywall circumvention and no Sci-Hub tier.

Local libraries created by this tool contain third-party PDFs. Those files are
data, are not part of this repository, and are not redistributed with it.
